  cli
    ⚠  WARN  ntfy-version  ntfy-version: could not probe version ("ntfy" --version exited 1) — version is unknown; upgrade to >= 2.21 (CVE-2026-39087, CVSS 9.8) to be safe
        fix: Upgrade ntfy to >= 2.21 (CVE-2026-39087 fix): see https://github.com/binwiederhier/ntfy/releases — stop container, pull new image, restart; or: brew upgrade ntfy 
    ⚠  WARN  tmux-version  tmux-version: could not probe version ("tmux" -V exited 1) — version is unknown; the session registry needs tmux >= 3.2 (D-27)
        fix: Upgrade tmux to >= 3.2 for session-typed notifications (D-27): brew upgrade tmux  (or your distro package manager); the daemon runs fine without it 
    ⚠  WARN  tailscale-version  tailscale-version: could not probe version ("tailscale" version exited 1) — version is unknown; upgrade Tailscale to >= 1.98.1 to meet the floor
        fix: Upgrade Tailscale to >= 1.98.1: brew upgrade tailscale  (or download from https://pkgs.tailscale.com) — below the floor is a fail-closed security gate 
    ⚠  WARN  nb-client-version  nb-client-version: could not probe version ("netbird" version exited 1) — version is unknown; upgrade NetBird (client) to >= 0.57.0 to meet the floor
        fix: Upgrade the NetBird client to >= 0.57.0: see https://github.com/netbirdio/netbird/releases  (or your package manager); below the floor is fail-closed 
    ⚠  WARN  et-version  et-version: could not probe version ("et" --version exited 1) — version is unknown; upgrade EternalTerminal to >= 6.2.0 to meet the floor
        fix: Upgrade EternalTerminal to >= 6.2.0 to prefer the ET transport: brew upgrade eternal-terminal  — advisory only; mosh remains a working fallback 
    ⚠  WARN  tailscale-statedir  tailscale-statedir: could not query Tailnet Lock status (tailscale lock status --json failed) — Lock-statedir posture unknown; ensure tailscaled is running then re-run abysslink doctor
        fix: Run tailscaled with a persistent statedir (systemd default /var/lib/tailscale, or set TS_STATE_DIR) — Tailnet Lock signing checks are not enforced without it; this is a fail-closed gate 
    ⚠  WARN  openssh-version  openssh-version: could not probe ssh version (ssh -V failed) — version unknown; install OpenSSH >= 10.0 for post-quantum KEX (mosh remains a working fallback)
        fix: Upgrade OpenSSH to >= 10.0 for post-quantum key exchange: brew upgrade openssh  (or your distro package manager) — advisory; mosh remains a working fallback 
    ⚠  WARN  openssh-pqkex  openssh-pqkex: could not probe ssh key-exchange algorithms (ssh -Q kex failed) — PQ-KEX support unknown; advisory only (mosh remains a working fallback)
        fix: Upgrade OpenSSH to >= 10.0 so ssh -Q kex lists mlkem768x25519-sha256 (post-quantum KEX) — advisory; mosh remains a working fallback 
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  content-store
    ⚠  WARN  content-store-daemon-down  abysslinkd not reachable — the credential pull and content fetch won't work (start it: abysslink daemon enable --apply)
        fix: Start the daemon: abysslink daemon enable --apply 
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  push-gateway
    ⚠  WARN  push-creds-keychain  abysslinkd not reachable — cannot verify gateway creds from daemon context (start it: abysslink daemon enable --apply)
